  Cell["Interior-generator multiplicity: open audit", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["A cancellation hypersurface is defined by non-monomial polynomial \
factors.  No x_i alone is treated as a cancellation factor.  The four \
full-support planar-hexbox vectors fall into three generator classes.  Rows 2 \
and 3 have the same product of the same two non-monomial linear factors (up \
to factor order and overall signs), but have different certified vectors.  \
Whether these are two genuinely distinct local facets of one singular \
hypersurface or an overcount remains to be established by a common \
local-coordinate/dissection analysis.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"row\"", "\"generator class\"", 
        "\"relative vector\"", "\"polynomial factor 1\"", 
